-## Edge cases
-- Round 1, nothing applied at Gate B: `plan.txt == plan.txt-original` → TIE → NOT_WORSE → no prompt; round-1 firing never blocks clean SIMPLE runs.
-- Round 1 prompt: PLAN_PREV duplicates PLAN_ORIGINAL — the new note tells assessors the Previous section repeats the anchor (FINDING_11).
-- Zero effective assessors: unchanged fail-open → NOT_WORSE with the `0/3` warning, no prompt.
-- SIMPLE multi-round (Gate-C re-runs, cap 3): cursor advances on SIMPLE; round N compares `plan.txt` vs `plan.txt-original`, `plan-after-round-(N-1).txt` as context.
-- Resumed SIMPLE session paused at `STEP=3b` (pre- or post-change): the dropped tier guard upgrades it to `3.6` so the assessor still fires (FINDING_8).
-- Resumed SIMPLE session with no `plan.txt-original` (created before this change): the missing-input guard settles `missing-snapshot` → skip, no crash.
+### Edge cases / failure modes
 
-## Failure modes
-- Orphaned-variable lint break: deleting a gate while leaving `WORKFLOW_PATH` / `_wp_round` trips shellcheck SC2034 and fails `make lint`. Mitigation: remove each orphaned resolution in the same edit; `make lint` is the signal.
-- Structure-pin / fixture drift: changing the Step 3.6 skip breadcrumb or `(HARD-only)` comment without updating `test-design-structure.sh` fails that harness. Mitigation: update every pin/fixture in the same change.
-- Pause-resume regression: relaxing the `3b` guard without a SIMPLE `test-design-pause-resume.sh` case ships an untested branch. Mitigation: add the SIMPLE case in the same change.
-- Doc/security drift: leaving SECURITY.md / plan-review.md / approval-gates.md HARD-only after enabling SIMPLE understates the trust surface. Mitigation: the doc edits above; pre-commit + structure harness catch pinned references.
